<title>CHINA: Shanghai grain exchange to close during holiday.</title>
<headline>Shanghai grain exchange to close during holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Cereals and Oils Exchange will close on Thursday and Friday for the Labour Day holiday, the exchange said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Trading will resume next Monday, it said.</p>
<p>The most actively traded September 1997 contract ended Wednesday at an intraday high of 3,385 yuan ($408) per tonne, rising 40 yuan. It opened at a low of 3,340 yuan.</p>
<p>($1=8.2948 yuan)</p>
</text>
